---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const tools = [
  { name: 'Daftra', status: 'Vendor says fully integrated with ETA (e-signature, GS1 codes, Egyptian VAT)', fit: 'Accounting / e-invoice SMEs', note: 'From $20/mo billed yearly (USD)', href: '/eg/daftra/' },
  { name: 'AccFlex', status: 'Vendor says ETA-approved; construction edition with مستخلصات', fit: 'SMEs incl. contractors', note: 'Small-business edition from the equivalent of US$29; larger edition quoted', href: '/eg/accflex-erp/' },
  { name: 'DoubleClick ERP', status: 'Vendor says it sends مستخلصات (payment certificates) and invoices to the ETA directly', fit: 'Contractors (engineering → finance)', note: 'Quote-based', href: '/eg/doubleclick-erp/' },
  { name: 'Voko ERP', status: 'Separate ETA e-invoice module + مستخلصات in its contracting module', fit: 'Contractors', note: 'Quote-based', href: '/eg/voko-erp/' },
  { name: 'Namasoft (NamaERP)', status: 'Vendor says it covers ETA e-invoices (HSM signing, GS1/EGS codes) and e-receipts', fit: 'Contractors and property firms (tenders, BOQs, payment certificates, retention)', note: 'Quote-based', href: '/eg/namasoft/' },
  { name: 'Edara', status: 'Egyptian e-invoicing in the Ultimate plan; vendor says it guides customers through ETA integration', fit: 'Trading and distribution SMEs', note: 'From $29/mo + $5/user billed yearly (USD); Ultimate $79 + $12/user', href: '/eg/edara-erp/' },
  { name: 'Odoo', status: 'Egyptian localization with an ETA e-invoicing module (API, GS1/EGS codes, USB-token signing), via partners', fit: 'Full ERP if you want one system', note: 'SaaS + implementation', href: '/eg/odoo/' },
  { name: 'OrchidaTax', status: 'ETA middleware/connector for SAP/Oracle/Dynamics/Odoo', fit: 'Keep your ERP, add compliance', note: 'Quote-based', href: '/eg/orchidatax/' },
  { name: 'QuickBooks', status: 'No ETA e-invoicing described by Intuit; needs a third-party connector (OrchidaTax lists QuickBooks)', fit: 'Firms already on QuickBooks', note: 'Connector priced separately', href: '/eg/quickbooks/' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is ETA e-invoicing mandatory yet, and for whom?', a: `Yes, for the taxpayers named in ETA's phased decisions. ETA made e-invoicing mandatory in phases: its inquiry page dates the obligation for phase 5 from 15 December 2021, phase 6 from 15 February 2022, phase 7 from 15 June 2022 and phase 8 in four sub-phases from 15 September to 15 December 2022. Its online inquiry tools show whether a particular business must use e-invoicing or e-receipts, so check your status there. ETA also runs a separate e-receipt system. The VAT registration threshold has been under review since late 2025, so none is stated here.` },
  { q: 'How are documents signed and checked?', a: 'ETA requires e-invoices to be electronically signed and sent through integration with its system, through your own software or one of the service providers it lists. The vendors in our directory describe the details: Daftra uses a signature certificate from Egypt Trust, Odoo signs with a USB token from the ETA or Egypt Trust, Namasoft describes HSM signing, and Odoo, Voko and Namasoft map products to GS1 or EGS codes. DoubleClick says it checks documents before sending and records the authority\'s validation afterwards. Ask your vendor to show the full submission working before you buy.' },
  { q: 'What happens if I don\'t comply?', a: 'ETA\'s pages read for this guide list its mandatory-implementation decisions but not the penalty amounts, so confirm the current penalties with ETA or your tax advisor. In the meantime, check your status with ETA\'s inquiry tool and make sure your software can sign e-invoices and send them through integration with ETA\'s system.' },
  { q: 'What format and what\'s the legal basis?', a: 'ETA\'s e-invoicing pages give guidance on electronic signature, integration with the e-invoicing system and item coding; vendors in our directory describe GS1 or EGS item codes and signing with an HSM or a USB token. VAT is levied under VAT Law No. 67 of 2016, amended in 2025 and 2026 (including Law 149/2026), and the Egyptian Tax Authority runs the e-invoicing and e-receipt systems.' },
  { q: 'Does my accounting software need to be ETA-native?', a: `If your business is covered by ETA's decisions, your software must reach the ETA somehow. Daftra, Edara (Ultimate plan), AccFlex, Namasoft and Voko say they submit to the ETA, DoubleClick says it sends مستخلصات and invoices directly, and Odoo has an Egyptian e-invoicing module. Intuit's global pages do not describe ETA e-invoicing for QuickBooks, so it needs a connector such as OrchidaTax, which lists QuickBooks among its integrations; Wafeq's Egypt pages make no ETA claim, so confirm with Wafeq. The right question for any vendor: "Do you submit documents to the ETA directly, or which connector do I need?"` },
  { q: 'What\'s the wider Egyptian tax context, and the FX angle?', a: 'The general VAT rate is 14%. For contractors, ETA lists Ministerial Decision 418/2025 on the tax basis for construction contracts, and October 2025 press reports describe 14% VAT being applied to contracting works, including existing contracts. Law 6/2025 gives tax incentives and simpler rules to projects with annual turnover up to EGP 20 million. On currency: Daftra, Edara, Odoo and PlanRadar list prices in USD, so their EGP cost moves with the exchange rate; Wafeq publishes EGP prices for Egypt.' },
];

const pageTitle = 'ETA E-Invoicing in Egypt: 2026 Guide for Contractors';
const pageDescription = `Egypt's ETA e-invoicing explained for the building trades: who must comply under ETA's phased decisions, how e-invoices are signed and sent, VAT on contracting works, and which tools say they submit to the ETA (incl. مستخلصات). Independent guide, updated October 2026.`;

const guideUrl = new URL('/eg/guides/eta-e-invoicing/', Astro.site).toString();
const arUrl = new URL('/eg/ar/guides/eta-e-invoicing/', Astro.site).toString();
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Egypt', url: '/eg/' },
  { name: 'ETA e-invoicing for contractors', url: '/eg/guides/eta-e-invoicing/' },
];

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: pageTitle, description: pageDescription,
  datePublished: '2026-06-20', dateModified: '2026-10-01', inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'WrenchStack Research', url: 'https://wrenchstack.com/research/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'WrenchStack', url: 'https://wrenchstack.com' },
  mainEntityOfPage: guideUrl,
};
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
};
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} alternateUrls={[{ hreflang: 'en', href: guideUrl }, { hreflang: 'ar', href: arUrl }, { hreflang: 'x-default', href: guideUrl }]}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <div class="mb-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-orange-600">🇪🇬 Egypt · Compliance guide</p>
        <a href="/eg/ar/guides/eta-e-invoicing/" class="rounded-md border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-50">العربية</a>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
        ETA E-Invoicing in Egypt
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        What Egypt's national e-invoicing means for the building trades: it is mandatory for the taxpayers named in ETA's phased decisions. Who must comply, how e-invoices are signed and sent, and which tools say they submit to the ETA (including مستخلصات).
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">By WrenchStack Research · Published June 2026, updated 1 October 2026 · Not tax advice; confirm your situation with the ETA (eta.gov.eg) or your accountant.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="mb-8 rounded-lg border-2 border-orange-300 bg-orange-50 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">⏰ The short version</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-800 leading-relaxed">
        Egypt's <strong>ETA e-invoicing</strong> is <strong>mandatory in phases</strong>: it applies to the taxpayers named in ETA's phased decisions (ETA's inquiry page dates the obligation for phase 5 from 15 December 2021 and for phase 8 in four sub-phases from 15 September to 15 December 2022), and ETA's online inquiry tool shows whether your business is covered. ETA requires e-invoices to be <strong>electronically signed</strong> and sent through integration with its system, through your own software or one of the service providers it lists. The task: check your status, then make sure your tool signs and submits to the ETA, directly or via a connector.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-center">
        <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Phased</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600">mandate by ETA decision; check with ETA's inquiry tool</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-center">
        <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">14%</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600">general VAT rate</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-center">
        <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">E-signature</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600">e-invoices signed and sent through integration with ETA's system</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 prose prose-slate max-w-none">
      <h2>The timeline</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>15 Dec 2021:</strong> e-invoicing obligation begins for phase 5, the taxpayers named in ETA's decision.</li>
        <li><strong>15 Feb 2022:</strong> phase 6 begins.</li>
        <li><strong>15 Jun 2022:</strong> phase 7 begins.</li>
        <li><strong>15 Sep-15 Dec 2022:</strong> phase 8, in four sub-phases starting on the 15th of each month.</li>
        <li><strong>2025-2026:</strong> VAT and tax procedure laws amended again (including Law 149/2026); ETA lists Ministerial Decision 418/2025 on the tax basis for construction contracts; the VAT registration threshold has been under review since late 2025.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the system requires</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Electronic signature.</strong> ETA requires e-invoices to be electronically signed; vendors in our directory describe an Egypt Trust certificate (Daftra), a USB token from the ETA or Egypt Trust (Odoo) or HSM signing (Namasoft).</li>
        <li><strong>Product coding.</strong> Odoo, Voko and Namasoft describe mapping products to GS1 or EGS codes, and ETA's e-invoicing pages give guidance on item coding.</li>
        <li><strong>Integration path.</strong> Integration with ETA's system through your own software or one of the service providers ETA lists, or a connector (such as OrchidaTax) for tools without an ETA module.</li>
        <li><strong>Check your scope.</strong> The mandate covers the taxpayers named in ETA's phased decisions; ETA's inquiry tool shows whether a business must use e-invoicing or e-receipts.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why this matters for contractors specifically</h2>
      <p>
        Contractors have their own tax points. ETA lists <strong>Ministerial Decision 418/2025</strong> on the tax basis for construction contracts, and October 2025 press reports describe <strong>14% VAT being applied to contracting works</strong>, including existing contracts. For <strong>مستخلصات (payment certificates)</strong>, <a href="/eg/doubleclick-erp/">DoubleClick</a> says it sends payment certificates and invoices to the ETA directly and prints the e-invoice QR code on the certificate, while <a href="/eg/voko-erp/">Voko</a>, Namasoft and AccFlex say their contracting modules handle payment certificates and that they support ETA e-invoicing. Check the currency too: Daftra, Edara and Odoo list prices in USD, so their EGP cost moves with the exchange rate.
      </p>

      <h2>The wider Egyptian tax context</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>VAT:</strong> general rate <strong>14%</strong>, per press reports on the 2025 and 2026 amendments.</li>
        <li><strong>Small projects:</strong> Law 6/2025 gives tax incentives and simpler rules to projects with annual turnover up to EGP 20 million.</li>
        <li><strong>The FX angle:</strong> tools priced in USD cost an EGP business more or less as the exchange rate moves.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Which tools are ETA-integrated?</h2>
      <p>
        From the software in our <a href="/eg/">Egypt directory</a>, here's how the tools relate to the ETA. Tools with an Egyptian e-invoicing module submit directly (Odoo has one through its Egyptian localization); tools without one, such as QuickBooks, need a connector. Always confirm current status with the vendor.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border border-slate-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        <thead class="bg-slate-50 text-left text-slate-700">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Tool</th>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">ETA status</th>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Fit</th>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Pricing</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 bg-white">
          {tools.map((t) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-slate-900"><a href={t.href} class="hover:text-orange-600">{t.name}</a></td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">{t.status}</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-600">{t.fit}</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-600">{t.note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">ETA status reflects what each vendor says, as checked in September 2026; confirm current ETA integration directly with each vendor.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">The one question to ask any vendor</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        Don't assume a good accounting tool submits to the ETA. And if you're a contractor, ask about مستخلصات too. Ask: <strong>"Do you submit documents to the ETA directly, do you handle مستخلصات, and do you price in EGP or USD?"</strong> A vague answer is your signal. If you're on QuickBooks, plan for a connector such as OrchidaTax, which lists QuickBooks among its integrations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="mb-5 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-slate-900">{f.q}</summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">{f.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 p-5 text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-slate-700">Sources &amp; verification:</strong> Phase dates from ETA's Arabic e-invoicing inquiry page (re-read 1 October 2026); the e-signature and integration requirement, the service-provider list, Ministerial Decision 418/2025, Law 6/2025 and the VAT law list (VAT Law No. 67 of 2016, Law 149/2026) from ETA's Arabic website, checked September 2026; the general 14% VAT rate and its application to contracting works from 2025-2026 press reports; vendor descriptions as each vendor publishes them, checked September 2026. Claims in the June 2026 version that rested on secondary sources (a real-time clearance model, JSON/XML and UUID details, penalty amounts and earlier rollout dates) were removed on 1 October 2026 because they could not be confirmed on ETA's own pages. The VAT registration threshold has been under review since late 2025, so none is stated here. General information, not tax advice. Spotted an error? <a href="/contact/" class="underline">Tell us</a>.
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900 p-8 text-white">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Compare Egyptian trades software & services</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">Independent reviews of Egyptian accounting and construction software, tender access, social-insurance payroll and Contractors All Risks insurance, with no pay-to-play.</p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/eg/" class="rounded-md bg-orange-500 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-orange-600">🇪🇬 Egypt directory →</a>
        <a href="/eg/compare/" class="rounded-md bg-white px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-100">Compare vendors</a>
        <a href="/for-vendors/" class="rounded-md border border-white/30 bg-white/10 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-white/20">Are you a vendor? Work with us</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
